# absent-one — pattern
@id absent-one  @kind pattern  @layer library  @author toine  @lang en

## summary
~ Someone who matters is gone. The carrier knows them, the player does not; the story is the slow reading of what they left, until the carrier understands what they were doing. The absent one never appears.

## roles
role absent : character : the one who is gone
role witness : character : the carrier, who knew them
role trace* : thing : something they left, read in place (attrs: fact, line)
role resting_place : thing : where their story stops
role truth_clue : fact : what must be seen before the truth can land
role truth : fact : what they were doing, the answer to the story's question
role understand_line : line : what the witness says when the truth lands

## facts_required
need absence : fact : why they are gone, stated once, never contradicted
need truth : fact : the answer, true from the start, revealed late

## principles
!! $absent never appears, speaks or is found alive.
~0.8 $witness speaks of $absent through small concrete things, never in eulogies.
? How much does $witness already suspect? -- little at first; each trace moves her a step, not to the end.

## rules
when look.at($trace) once -> reveal($trace.fact), say($trace.line) {trace-read}
when look.at($resting_place) once if fact($truth_clue) -> reveal($truth), say($understand_line) {truth-lands}

## beats_hint
hint first beat: one trace that only the witness can read
hint middle beat: a trace that asks a choice of the player
hint last beat: the resting place; the truth lands on the witness, not on the player

## variations
variation alive : the absent one is only missing; the last beat may find them (changes the absolute, needs a visible character)
variation unknown : the witness did not know them either; the player and the witness read the traces together
